usb: chipidea: i.MX23: do not disable streaming mode

Setting USBMODE.SDIS on i.MX23 forces a full TX FIFO pre-fill and makes
the device answer every received packet with NYET in high-speed mode.
Sustained IN transfers (e.g. an RNDIS download from the target) hang
with it set. The i.MX23 reference manual does not require it.

diff -urN a/drivers/usb/chipidea/ci_hdrc_imx.c b/drivers/usb/chipidea/ci_hdrc_imx.c
--- a/drivers/usb/chipidea/ci_hdrc_imx.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/chipidea/ci_hdrc_imx.c
@@ -24,8 +24,7 @@
 };
 
 static const struct ci_hdrc_imx_platform_flag imx23_usb_data = {
-	.flags = CI_HDRC_TURN_VBUS_EARLY_ON |
-		CI_HDRC_DISABLE_STREAMING,
+	.flags = CI_HDRC_TURN_VBUS_EARLY_ON,
 };
 
 static const struct ci_hdrc_imx_platform_flag imx27_usb_data = {
